      "verseNumber": 7,
      "subDivision": "Pratyabhijñā Sūtras (1–20)",
      "devanagari": "स च द्विरूपस्त्रिमलश्चतुरावृतः पञ्चकृत्यकारी सप्तपञ्चकस्वभावः ॥ ७ ॥",
      "iast": "sa ca dvirūpas trimalaś caturāvṛtaḥ pañcakṛtyakārī saptapañcakasvabhāvaḥ || 7 ||",
      "padaccheda": [
        {
          "wordDevanagari": "सः",
          "wordIast": "saḥ",
          "grammaticalRole": "nom. sg. m.",
          "literalMeaning": "he (the bound soul)"
        },
        {
          "wordDevanagari": "द्विरूपः",
          "wordIast": "dvirūpaḥ",
          "grammaticalRole": "nom. sg. m.",
          "literalMeaning": "two-formed (divine essence and contracted appearance)"
        },
        {
          "wordDevanagari": "त्रिमलः",
          "wordIast": "trimalaḥ",
          "grammaticalRole": "nom. sg. m.",
          "literalMeaning": "possessing three impurities (āṇava, māyīya, kārma)"
        },
        {
          "wordDevanagari": "चतुरावृतः",
          "wordIast": "catur-āvṛtaḥ",
          "grammaticalRole": "nom. sg. m.",
          "literalMeaning": "covered by four sheaths"
        },
        {
          "wordDevanagari": "पञ्चकृत्यकारी",
          "wordIast": "pañcakṛtyakārī",
          "grammaticalRole": "nom. sg. m.",
          "literalMeaning": "performing the five cosmic acts"
        },
        {
          "wordDevanagari": "सप्तपञ्चकस्वभावः",
          "wordIast": "saptapañcakasvabhāvaḥ",
          "grammaticalRole": "nom. sg. m.",
          "literalMeaning": "having the nature of the thirty-five tattvas"
        }
      ],
      "studyGloss": "And that bound subject is twofold in nature, covered by the three impurities, enveloped by four veils, perpetually performing the five cosmic acts, and embodying the thirty-five tattvas.",
      "practicalContext": "A crucial taxonomic sūtra integrating the entire metaphysics of Trika into the anatomy of the human person.",
